# lf116, the river-stone taproom keeper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf116
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent light broad
tier full
written_for tn_cw_bramble_reedford
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the river-stone taproom keeper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=innkeeper
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk collects_smooth_stones_from_the_riverbanks
likes fried_fish riddles new_boots first_warm_day
dislikes night_noise drizzle
fears an_empty_taproom_after_a_bad_harvest a_guest_left_alone_on_the_road
hopes every_guest_finds_a_bed a_quiet_morning_after_the_last_cart
topics work +0.4 home +0.4 travel +0.3 faith +0.2
styles comfort=steady gossip=discreet refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps the #taproom# warm, collects smooth #stones# by the #river#, and answers a hard #night# with a dry #riddle#.

words
oath! = By the river stones | Bright One keep the hearth
saying! = A clean cup needs no story | Let the guest finish the riddle
taproom = taproom | quiet taproom
inn = inn | small inn
room = room | upstairs room
rooms = rooms | upstairs rooms
bed = bed | clean bed
beds = beds | made beds
key = key | room key
keys = keys | room keys
guest = guest | road guest
guests = guests | overnight guests
traveller = traveller | tired traveller
stranger = stranger | passing stranger
friend = friend | close friend
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
helper = helper | pot hand
counter = counter | taproom counter
tap = tap | ale tap
cask = cask | ale cask
casks = casks | stored casks
ale = ale | small ale
cup = cup | clean cup
cups = cups | washed cups
mug = mug | clay mug
mugs = mugs | clay mugs
pot = pot | kitchen pot
pots = pots | washed pots
plate = plate | supper plate
plates = plates | empty plates
bread = bread | fresh bread
fish = fish | fried fish
butter = butter | melted butter
meal = meal | hot meal
supper = supper | late supper
hearth = hearth | taproom hearth
fire = fire | banked fire
wood = wood | dry wood
bench = bench | long bench
table = table | shared table
seat = seat | corner seat
floor = floor | scrubbed floor
stair = stair | narrow stair
stairs = stairs | upstairs steps
door = door | front door
voice = voice | low voice
log = log | dry log
nights = nights | hard nights
nightfall = nightfall | late nightfall
mornings = mornings | early mornings
travellers = travellers | road travellers
house = house | great house
cost = cost | honest cost
window = window | small window
roof = roof | sound roof
flat = flat | upstairs flat
ledger = ledger | room ledger
book = book | guest book
name = name | guest name
names = names | guest names
price = price | room price
coin = coin | counted coin
wage = wage | honest wage
road = road | long road
mile = mile | slow mile
miles = miles | unwelcome miles
cart = cart | supply cart
wagon = wagon | goods wagon
wheel = wheel | cart wheel
city = city | far city
market = market | city market
river = river | near river
bank = bank | river bank
banks = banks | river banks
stone = stone | smooth stone
stones = stones | smooth stones
riddle = riddle | short riddle
answer = answer | riddle answer
question = question | riddle question
boot = boot | new boot
boots = boots | dry boots
spring = spring | early spring
warmth = warmth | first warmth
day = day | warm day
morning = morning | quiet morning
evening = evening | late evening
night = night | noisy night
noise = noise | late noise
drizzle = drizzle | thin drizzle
rain = rain | steady rain
mud = mud | road mud
lamp = lamp | door lamp
watch = watch | town watch
festival = festival | town festival
prayer = prayer | quiet prayer
light = light | hearth light
larder = larder | inn larder
store = store | supply store
order = order | guest order
work = work | inn work
queue = queue | waiting queue

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : I speak a #prayer# while turning the #key# each #morning#. | I keep a #bed# for a weary pilgrim.
opinion @1 city against 1 : I have carried #casks# toward the #city# and begrudged every #mile#. | Its #market# forgets the small inns.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Feed a hungry #guest# before weighing the reason. | An empty #plate# is plain enough.
opinion @1 drink mixed 1 : A #cup# can bring a #traveller# to speak freely. | I cut off anyone who turns loud after dark.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : I would rather watch the crowd pass from this #window#. | The #floor# needs cleaning afterward.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A grand #house# has more #rooms# than I can name. | Its doors have never opened to my #guests#.
opinion @1 road against 1 : A late #cart# leaves the #larder# thin. | I know the #road# well enough to blame its ruts.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A #stranger# can have a #meal# before giving a #name#. | That is how I keep this #taproom#.
opinion @1 times against 1 : The same #coin# now buys less #bread#. | My #guests# feel it at the #counter#.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : The #watch# makes the #road# safer after #nightfall#. | I still keep the #lamp# lit.
line @1 greet : #greet#. There is a #seat# near the #hearth#. | #greet#. Tell me if you need a #bed#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I kept the smaller #cup# for you. | Come in before the #pot# is empty.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The #fire# lasted the #night#. | I have already counted the #keys#.
line @1 greet.return : The #riddle# remains unsolved, if you want another try. | Your #seat# is free again.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I have saved #bread# beside the #pot#. | Come upstairs when the #guests# settle.
line @1 again.open : I was counting the #keys#. | Did you answer the #riddle#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Shut the #door# gently. | Take care on the #road# beyond the #lamp#.
line @1 farewell.return : Another #cup# will be ready if you return. | Perhaps you will bring a better #riddle#.
line @1 react.news : Speak low; the #guests# are resting. | This #cup# can wait; I am listening.
line @1 react.news.new : I have heard no such news across this #counter#. | Was it brought along the #road#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a little of it from a #traveller#. | You have given me the middle of the tale.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would ask who kept the #key# that #night#. | Did anyone watch that #guest# leave the #room#?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry; take the quiet #seat# by the #fire#. | I can find you a quiet #room# tonight.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A good day deserves #fish# from the #pot#. | I will fetch a clean #cup#.
line @1 answer.how : The #taproom# held together through the #night#. | Better with the #store# stocked.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I must serve this #guest# first. | Let me finish counting the #keys#.
line @1 ask.how : Were you kept dry by a #roof# last #night#? | Did your #boots# survive the #road#?
line @1 sympathise : Take the #seat# furthest from the #noise#. | I can bring a #meal# without questions.
line @1 reassure : The #lamp# will stay lit until you come in. | We can put another #log# on the #fire#.
line @1 decline : I cannot give out a #key# without a #room# free. | I will not serve another #cup# to a loud #guest#.
line @1 accept_decline : Understood. I will put that #cup# away. | Then we can leave the #room# unbooked.
line @1 thank : You carried the #cask# to the #store# for me. | The #fish# was well cooked tonight.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I only had to find a clean #plate#. | The #door# was open already.
line @1 preclose : I must bank the #fire# before I rest. | The last #guest# needs a #key#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : Your #riddle# has more corners than my #stairs#. | You polish a #stone# by carrying it, not talking to it.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #room# is ready. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will check the #book#.
line @1 give.advice : Keep a dry pair of #boots# when the #road# is wet. | Ask for a #bed# before the late #cart# arrives.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay under the #lamp# until company comes. | Take the #road# with other #travellers#.
scene clean_cup
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A clean #cup# tells a #guest# I noticed them. | I check the rim before setting it on the #counter#.
b : Do guests notice? | Who washes them?
a : Some do. | The #hands# take turns.

scene cask_tap
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I tap a #cask# gently so the first #ale# runs clear. | A hard knock stirs what should stay at the bottom.
b : Do you waste any? | Who sets the cask?
a : Only the first pour. | I do when it arrives.

scene room_key
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Every #key# has a mark I can feel in the dark. | I keep them in the same order by the #book#.
b : Has one gone missing? | Can you tell them apart?
a : Once, briefly. | With my eyes closed.

scene night_ledger
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count #rooms# against the #ledger# before I close the #counter#. | A #guest# should not find another person in the #bed#.
b : Has that happened? | Do you check twice?
a : Not in this inn. | Each #night#.

scene banked_fire
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #fire# must stay warm without throwing sparks toward the #bench#. | I bank it after the last #cup#.
b : Does it last till morning? | Who rises first?
a : Most nights. | Whoever hears the #cart#.

scene pot_hand
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #pots# come back from the #table# in every condition. | A good #hand# can make them ready by #morning#.
b : Does it take long? | Do you help?
a : Until the final #plate#. | Whenever the room quiets.

scene late_guest
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #traveller# reached the #door# after the #lamp# had burned low. | I found a #room# and let the questions wait.
b : Did they stay? | Did they pay?
a : For one #night#. | In the #morning#.

scene quiet_seat
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #seat# near the #window# stays empty until the late #guests# arrive. | It is a place to recover from the #road#.
b : Do you sit there? | Does it have a view?
a : After closing. | The #river# bend.

scene river_stone
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I collect smooth #stones# along the #river# #bank#. | One fits in my palm like an old #key#.
b : What do you do with them? | How many have you found?
a : Keep a few upstairs. | Enough to stop counting.

scene stone_choice
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The best #stone# is one the #river# has rounded without cracking. | I leave rough ones where they lie.
b : Why collect them? | Do guests see them?
a : They settle in the #hand#. | Only if they ask.

scene short_riddle
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A short #riddle# can quiet a #table# faster than a sharp word. | I give the #answer# after supper.
b : Do people guess it? | What is the prize?
a : Some do. | The satisfaction.

scene wrong_answer
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #guest# gave me a better #answer# than the one I knew. | I kept the #riddle# and changed its ending.
b : Do you remember it? | Did they win something?
a : Yes; it made me laugh. | The last piece of #bread#.

scene fried_fish
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #plate# of #fish# fried in #butter# travels quickly across this room. | I eat mine after the #guests#.
b : Do you cook it? | Does any remain?
a : When the #pot# is free. | Rarely.

scene first_warm_day
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : On the first warm #day# of #spring# I open the #door# wide. | The #taproom# smells of #river# air instead of old #wood#.
b : Do you close it at night? | Do guests like it?
a : When the light goes. | The quiet ones do.

scene thin_drizzle
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Thin #drizzle# brings #mud# in on every pair of #boots#. | It never seems enough to wash the #road# clean.
b : Do you mind wiping it? | Does it last?
a : It is part of the #work#. | Far too long.

scene night_noise
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A shout after #nightfall# carries from the #counter# to every #room#. | I ask the loud #guest# to finish their #cup# outside.
b : Do they listen? | What if they refuse?
a : Usually. | The #watch# is close.

scene cart_to_city
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I took a load of #casks# by #cart# toward the #city#. | Each #mile# felt longer on the return.
b : Why take the load yourself? | Will you go again?
a : To keep the #wheel# moving. | Only if I must.

scene road_rut
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A deep rut kept the #cart# still while the #larder# at home emptied. | I remember its place better than the #market# gate.
b : Did you free it? | Who repaired the road?
a : Before dark. | No one then.

scene room_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I write the #price# plainly beside the #book#. | A tired #guest# should not have to bargain at #night#.
b : Does it change? | What about a week?
a : Only when costs do. | The #book# gives that price.

scene bread_for_hungry
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : If a #traveller# has no #coin#, I can still put #bread# on a #plate#. | A quiet #prayer# has never filled a stomach alone.
b : Do you ask for payment later? | Who taught you that?
a : Only if they can. | Hard #nights# taught me.

scene morning_prayer
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I say a small #prayer# while opening the #door#. | It is brief enough not to delay the #guests#.
b : Do you pray every day? | Does anyone join you?
a : Most #mornings#. | Sometimes a #hand#.

scene watch_at_door
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #watch# passes beneath the #lamp# after the #taproom# settles. | I hear their steps as I put away the #keys#.
b : Do you call to the #watch#? | Is the road safe?
a : When there is need. | Safer with a light.

scene festival_table
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #festival# fills each #bench# with people talking over one another. | I wait for its last #cup# before I enjoy the day.
b : Do you ever join in? | Is it profitable?
a : From the #window#. | Enough to pay the #hands#.

scene new_boots
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : New #boots# make the walk to the #river# feel like a short errand. | I keep the old ones for carrying #casks#.
b : Do you wear them often? | Why keep both?
a : When the #road# is dry. | The old pair still works.

scene guest_names
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I write a #name# in the #book# only after I have found the #room#. | People rest more easily when they know the #key# is real.
b : Do you remember names? | Do you ever turn someone away?
a : Some. | When all #beds# are taken.

scene city_market
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #city# #market# was louder than the full #taproom#. | I wanted the #river# and its smooth #stones# before noon.
b : Did you buy anything? | Did you return quickly?
a : What the #store# needed. | As soon as the #cart# was ready.

scene last_cup
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I leave one clean #cup# behind the #counter# for a late arrival. | It saves a clatter when the #rooms# are asleep.
b : Do you always need it? | Who gets it?
a : Often enough. | Whoever reaches the #door# last.

story first_key [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : A #guest# returned a #key# I thought had vanished.
  : It had been under the #plate# beside their #bed#.
  ask : Were you relieved?
  b : An odd place for it.
  : I put a brighter mark on that #key#.

story river_pocket [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : I carried a smooth #stone# from the #river# in my pocket.
  : It wore a hole through the cloth before I noticed.
  ask : Did you keep it?
  b : A costly little stone.
  : It sits beside the #lamp# now.

story city_cart [topic=travel self.age>=18]
  : I went to the #city# with a #cart# of supplies.
  : A rut held the #wheel# while the #taproom# ran short at home.
  ask : Did you reach them in time?
  b : A hard way to buy supplies.
  : Before the last #cask# emptied.

story riddle_guest [topic=pastimes self.age>=18]
  : A #traveller# answered my #riddle# before I had finished it.
  : The whole #table# fell quiet for a moment.
  ask : What was the answer?
  b : A quick mind.
  : A #stone# that had never touched the #river#.

story late_bread [topic=faith self.age>=18]
  : Someone came to the #door# without #coin# after #nightfall#.
  : I brought #bread# and left a #bed# ready without asking why.
  ask : Did they stay?
  b : That was kind.
  : Until the first #morning# #cart#.

rule @bark_cup
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say This #cup# still has a mark. | Bring a clean one to the #counter#.

rule @bark_key
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say The #key# for that #room# is here. | Count the #keys# before the #door# closes.

rule @bark_stone
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say I found another smooth #stone#. | The #river# did the polishing.

rule @bark_riddle
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say I owe you a #riddle#. | Give me your #answer# after supper.

rule @bark_fire
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Put one more piece of #wood# on. | The #fire# is settling.

rule @bark_night
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 13h
say Keep your #voice# low near the #stairs#. | The #guests# have gone to bed.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I can find you a #seat#. | #greet#. The #pot# is warm.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Your last #riddle# still bothers me. | The #cup# you favored is clean.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Speak softly; the #rooms# are occupied. | I can hear you by the #lamp#.
dlg @1 resident.job : I keep the #taproom# at #self.workplace#. | I manage #beds#, #casks#, and the #guest# #book#.
dlg @2 resident.job [self.working=yes] : I am counting #keys# for the #rooms#. | That #cask# needs a careful tap.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I will bank the #fire#. | #saying.capitalize#. Mind the #stair#.
dlg @1 inn.greet [here.inn_helper!=yes here.shop!=asleep] : #greet#. A #bed#, a #meal#, or a quiet #seat#? | Come beneath the #lamp# and say whether you need rest or supper.
dlg @2 inn.greet [topic.meeting=known here.inn_helper!=yes here.shop!=asleep] : You know the #taproom# now. | The #bench# you used before is clear.
dlg @3 inn.greet [here.inn_helper=yes] : I can find you food; ask #here.innkeeper# about a #bed#. | The #pot# is mine, but the #keys# belong to #here.innkeeper#.
dlg @1 inn.rooms : A #bed# is #here.bed_night#p tonight or #here.bed_week#p for the week. | The upstairs is #here.upstairs_night#p if all #rooms# are free.
dlg @1 inn.roomed : Here is your #key#; the #stairs# are by the #hearth#. | Your #room# is ready. Leave wet #boots# below.
dlg @1 inn.bye : #farewell#. Set the #key# on the #counter# when you go. | The #lamp# will stay lit for the #road#.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : #greet#. There is #fish# from the #pot# and #ale# in the #cask#. | Ask me the #price# before you order.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : The #larder# is thin today. | I can pour a #cup# while the #cart# is due.
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : The #counter# is closed for a short rest. | Return after I have warmed the #pot#.
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare here.shop!=asleep] : #greet#. I can tell you what the #pot# holds. | The #counter# is open; choose a #cup#.
dlg @1 shop.prices [here.shop=open|bare] : The #price# is marked by the #counter#. | I can explain the #cost# of a #meal# or a #room#.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #farewell#. Mind your #cup# on the way out. | #shop_bye# I will set another #plate#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why keep river stones? -> stones
node stones
say The #river# rounds them with no help from me. I keep a few upstairs.
free
choice Have you a riddle? -> riddle
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node riddle
say What travels the #road# but never enters the #inn#? A cart rut.
choice Back to the taproom. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft inn.greet
choice Is there a bed tonight? -> beds
node beds
say I will check the #book# and show you the #rooms# before taking #coin#.
free
choice What is for supper? -> supper
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node supper
say There is #fish# from the #pot# if the last #guest# has not claimed it.
choice Back to the counter. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #hearth# has just caught. | #greet#. I have a #key# free tonight.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The last #cup# is washed. | I will leave the #lamp# lit awhile.
